# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; this file is not.

# ─── Brandfetch Logo API ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT a secret. Brandfetch require the client ID to be embedded in the
# <img src> of a live page, so it ships in the HTML and every visitor can
# read it. Renaming it does not change that.
#
# No PUBLIC_ prefix needed. That prefix exists so client-side JavaScript can
# read a value from import.meta.env; this one is interpolated into the markup
# by ClientMarquee.astro at build time, so it is already in the HTML by the
# time a browser sees the page. (An earlier note here claimed the prefix was
# required — it was not.)
#
# Because it has no prefix, Vite does not inject it into import.meta.env, so
# the component reads process.env first. That is what lets a value set in the
# Vercel dashboard reach the build.
#
# It still belongs in an env var rather than hardcoded, so local and
# production can differ and so it can be rotated without a code change.
#
# Get one free: https://developers.brandfetch.com/register
BRANDFETCH_CLIENT_ID=

# ─── Contact form ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THIS ONE IS A SECRET. No PUBLIC_ prefix — it must stay server-side, and
# is read by the contact API route at request time, not by Astro at build time.
# Set it in the Vercel project's environment variables, never in the repo.
CONTACT_WEBHOOK_URL=
